From: Funkyhacks <funkyhacks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] api/file_routes: RFC 6266 Content-Disposition (no header breakout)

file_content() set Content-Disposition: inline; filename="<name>" where
name is the attacker-controlled decrypted original name. A filename with an
embedded quote breaks out of the value (header breakout / proxy-smuggling
surface; Starlette/h11 block raw CRLF so it is not full injection). Emit a
safe ASCII fallback plus a UTF-8 filename* per RFC 6266 section 4.

Refs: docs/SECURITY.md finding (Content-Disposition), THREAT-MODEL.md T18.

---
--- a/app/api/file_routes.py
+++ b/app/api/file_routes.py
@@ -44,6 +44,31 @@
     return guessed or fallback
 
 
+# EXACT target text for the 0006 patch (self-contained function, verified).
+# The generator reads this file and splices in the function below.
+
+def _content_disposition(filename: str) -> str:
+    """Build an RFC 6266 Content-Disposition value from an untrusted filename.
+
+    The decrypted original name is attacker-controlled (set at upload). The
+    old code interpolated it raw into ``filename="..."``, so a value like
+    ``x"; Set-Cookie: evil=1; filename="y`` breaks out of the quoted string
+    (SECURITY.md finding: Content-Disposition injection). Starlette/h11 reject
+    raw CRLF so it is not a full header-injection, but it is a malformed-header
+    / proxy-smuggling surface. Emit a safe ASCII fallback plus a UTF-8
+    ``filename*`` per RFC 6266 section 4.
+    """
+    import urllib.parse
+
+    unsafe = set('";\r\n\t') | set(chr(i) for i in range(0, 32))
+    safe = "".join(c if (c.isascii() and c not in unsafe) else "_" for c in filename).strip()
+    if not safe:
+        safe = "download"
+    encoded = urllib.parse.quote(filename, safe="")
+    return 'inline; filename="' + safe + '"; filename*=UTF-8\'\'' + encoded
+
+
+
 def _ext_of(filename: str) -> str:
     _, ext = os.path.splitext(filename)
     return ext.lstrip(".").lower() or "bin"

--- a/app/api/file_routes.py
+++ b/app/api/file_routes.py
@@ -176,7 +176,7 @@
         media_type=rec.content_type,
         headers={
             "Content-Length": str(rec.size),
-            "Content-Disposition": f'inline; filename="{name}"',
+            "Content-Disposition": _content_disposition(name),
             "Cache-Control": "no-store",
         },
     )
